hi this is presh tallaker let's learn  how to multiply numbers that are close  to 100 in your head  let's do 97 times 96 there are three  steps to the process  the first step is to write down the  difference from 100 97 is 3 less than  196 is 4 less  the second step is to cross subtract 97  minus 4 is 93  you'll notice that if you cross subtract  the other way it's the same answer  the final step is to cross multiply  three times four is twelve and that's  our answer nine thousand three hundred  and twelve  let's do another example ninety-eight  times ninety-three  we first take the difference from a  hundred of each number  then we cross subtract  and finally we cross multiply  and then we get our answer  9114  we can also do this for numbers that are  in the 80s it's exactly the same steps  we take the difference from 100 we cross  subtract  and then finally we cross multiply  the same  similar process will work if the two  numbers are above a hundred  you take the difference from a hundred  but now the only difference is we will  cross add a hundred and seven plus four  is a hundred and eleven we still cross  multiply and that's our answer  here's a quick proof of why this works  in general our multiplication problems  have been a hundred minus x times a  hundred minus y  we can write it in this form 100 minus x  minus y is cross subtract and the xy is  the cross multiply please subscribe to  my channel  you can support me on patreon  catch me on my blog mind your decisions  on twitter at preshtalwalkar  and you can get my books and amazon
 

